WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.588
This practice refines the billing CASE by giving an
exact zero bill

00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:09.262
its own category The order is deliberate Check NULL
first so missing

00:00:09.288 --> 00:00:14.600
values are not confused with zero Then check
bill_amount equals zero and

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:19.175
label it No Charge After that test the high and
standard thresholds

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.650
and use ELSE for the remaining positive low-value
bills Run the query

00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:28.975
and inspect patient 107 whose bill is exactly zero
That record should

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.925
now show No Charge rather than Low-Value This
demonstrates how domain meaning

00:00:33.938 --> 00:00:35.175
affects branch design
